      "answerKeyShort": "6x^3+6x^2-14x+17, 3",
      "resultDegree": 3,
      "sourceEvidence": {
        "enPrintedPage": 87,
        "enPdfPage": 93,
        "answerEnPrintedPage": 310,
        "answerEnPdfPage": 316
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "reason": "Write the sum p(x) + q(x) and group like powers of x in descending order from x³ down to the constant term.",
          "equation": "p(x) + q(x) = 6x³ + 6x² + (−7x − 7x) + (2 + 15)",
          "mathLatex": "p(x)+q(x)=6x^3+6x^2+(-7x-7x)+(2+15)"
        },
        {
          "reason": "Add the coefficients of the like terms: −7 − 7 = −14 for x, and 2 + 15 = 17 for the constant.",
          "equation": "p(x) + q(x) = 6x³ + 6x² − 14x + 17",
          "mathLatex": "p(x)+q(x)=6x^3+6x^2-14x+17"
        },
        {
          "reason": "The highest power of x with a nonzero coefficient in the resultant polynomial is x³, so its degree is 3.",
          "equation": "degree = 3",
          "mathLatex": "\\deg=3"
        }
      ],
